<file path="arq/DEBUGGING.md">
# ARQ debugging

เริ่มจาก evidence อย่าเปลี่ยน timing แบบสุ่ม. `STATUS` replays startup,
build/config identity, counters, last result and RTT diagnostics.

| Symptom | Check |
| --- | --- |
| No command ACK | UPDI owner, mailbox connection, newline, bounded hex syntax; both boards must ARM same session |
| BOOT rc nonzero / ready=0 | RegVersion, SPI route generated from pin TOML, receiver power enable, PA_BOOST and RadioLib return codes |
| No DATA | Unarmed/stopped Sender, SEND syntax, one outstanding transaction, 3 s spacing |
| DATA but no ACK | CRC counter, exact case-sensitive Hello World, peer IDs/session/sequence, RX restoration, TX errors |
| REJECTED | Wrong application bytes; expected for H02; new session before another request |
| PROTOCOL_ERROR | Receiver expected sequence differs; do not force RF to change session; re-arm both with fresh session |
| TIMEOUT_EXHAUSTED | Five attempts maximum; inspect immutable DATA and exponential intervals; separate suppression from RF loss |
| Missing/partial lines | `overflow`, disconnected logger, UPDI byte readiness; trial invalid, protocol must still progress |
| Duplicate application delivery | Acceptance/dedup state lost by reset, or wrong payload-validation ordering; invalidate trial on reset |

`python tools/arq_trial.py --validate <bundle.json>` checks file integrity and
exchange completeness, not authenticity. Keep acquired bundles and simulated
fixtures separate. Raw logs alone are insufficient proof of physical RF.
Use full-memory snapshots before any recovery; never erase whole Flash or
alter fuses/BOOTSIZE/EEPROM to repair an ARQ test. Existing bounded application
writer is reused; no changes to UPDI programming protocol.

RTT is one MCU's TxDone-to-ACK interval, first attempts only. Compare sample
counts and local timestamps; never subtract Receiver and Sender clocks.
Power integrity has not been measured. Deduplication does not survive reset.

## UPDI register evidence

`REG`, `TX_STATE` and Sender `RX_STATE` contain bytes read directly over SPI,
in this address order (not a protocol frame):

`01 06 07 08 09 4D 1D 1E 26 39 33 3B 12 13 10 1B 40 11 18 31`.

| Offset | Register | Interpretation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | OpMode 01 | Bit 7 LoRa; mode bits 2:0 = 3 TX, 5 continuous RX |
| 1–3 | Frf 06–08 | E4 C0 00 = 915 MHz with 32 MHz reference |
| 4–5 | PA_CONFIG / PA_DAC | F0 / 84 = selected 2 dBm PA_BOOST profile |
| 6–11 | Modem1 / Modem2 / Modem3 / sync / IQ / IQ2 | 72 / 74 / 04 / 12 / 27 / 1D |
| 12 | IrqFlags 12 | RxDone 40; payload CRC error 20; TxDone 08 |
| 13–15 | RxNbBytes / FIFO RX current / RSSI value | Raw receive/FIFO/noise observations |
| 16 | DioMapping1 40 | DIO0 bits 7:6 = 00 RxDone, 01 TxDone; IRQ polling does not require DIO interrupts |
| 17–19 | IrqFlagsMask / ModemStatus / DetectOptimize | Raw IRQ mask, modem activity, detector configuration |

`RX_READY rc=0` follows the actual `startReceive()` return. Compare local
TX_DONE → RX_READY/RX_STATE times to test the turnaround boundary. Consult the
[Semtech SX1276 datasheet](https://core-electronics.com.au/attachments/localcontent/SX1276_Datasheet_52573f9f913.pdf)
for register definitions. RegVersion does not prove the physical module's
frequency variant or its antenna connection.

Sender board schematic routes ANT to SMA through SB1 or U.FL through SB2;
an attached antenna also needs the corresponding bridge closed. See
[Gateway SSOT](../ssot/GATEWAY_SSOT.md). The operator confirmed approximately
one metre indoor separation on 2026-11-13. Later clarification supersedes
the earlier antenna assumption: installed connector, SB1/SB2 continuity,
antenna attachment and actual module/frequency marking are **PHYSICAL
INSPECTION REQUIRED**. BOM/schematic specify RFM95W; they do not verify the
populated module. Do not transmit again until the operator confirms inspection.
</file>

<file path="arq/PROTOCOL.md">
# Raw LoRa ARQ V1

ทั้งสองบอร์ดเริ่มแบบ unarmed ใน standby; host ต้อง ARM session ใหม่หลัง reset เสมอ.
Raw MVP และ legacy `src/ssot.c` ยังคงเดิม.

Wire bytes: version=1, type (DATA=1/ACK=2/NACK=3), source, destination,
session uint32 LE, sequence uint16 LE, payload length, reason, payload.
Header=12 bytes, payload<=32, frame<=44. DATA/ACK reason=0; ACK/NACK
payload empty. NACK reason: 1 unexpected sequence, 2 application rejected,
3 temporarily busy. Malformed/CRC/address/session failures are silent.

Commands are newline terminated, bounded ASCII: `ARM 1234ABCD`,
`SEND 48656C6C6F20576F726C64`, `STATUS`, `X`, and test receiver only
`FAULT 10 10`. ARM same session is idempotent; session replacement while
active is rejected. RF cannot arm devices. X stops new requests, lets an
outstanding request finish, then parks the radio in standby. A new-session
ARM clears stop and enables RX. Host reserves sessions
monotonically on disk and waits for both ARM acknowledgements.

Sender: IDLE -> TRANSMITTING -> WAITING_ACK -> BACKOFF -> TRANSMITTING.
DELIVERED/FAILED retain result until explicit SEND. One immutable outstanding
frame, initial RTO sampled once in [2000,3000] ms, doubles each retry, four
retries. TxDone/cleanup/RX success precede RTO start. Controls are processed
before deadlines. Matching ACK in WAITING_ACK/BACKOFF succeeds; matching
application rejection -> REJECTED, unexpected sequence -> PROTOCOL_ERROR.
BUSY uses the existing deadline (repetition cannot postpone retry).
No second full wait in BACKOFF after timeout; DATA starts >=3000 ms apart.
TX timeout=3000 ms, fatal adapter failure -> RADIO_ERROR, exhausted budget
-> TIMEOUT_EXHAUSTED. Fixed transaction deadline bounds all attempts,
including local TX and spacing. All intervals stay below half uint32 range.
Sequence increments only on ACK, modulo 65536; sequence reuse requires a
new session, including after a failed transaction. Reset aborts the trial.

Receiver: LISTENING -> VALIDATING -> SENDING_RESPONSE -> RETURNING_TO_RX
-> LISTENING. Exact configured payload accepted at expected sequence;
record acceptance before response. Duplicate last accepted DATA replays ACK,
without another delivery, only after exact payload validation. ACK failure
does not erase deduplication. Initial response guard=75 ms; subsequent guard
experiments come only from TOML with recorded evidence. Restore RX after response
or recoverable error; controls never produce controls. Fault injection drops
only selected first acceptance responses; duplicate replay remains enabled.

Diagnostics use 16 fixed event slots, nonblocking byte flushing, retained
startup/status, overflow count. RTT is local TxDone to matching ACK, only
without retransmission. Report samples/count/min/max/average/P95. No clock
subtraction between boards. Reset, overflow, missing terminal invalidates
completeness. STATUS_END follows all diagnostics and carries the final overflow
count; the host waits for that marker in the active session before closing.
Text parser validation alone cannot prove physical origin.

Deferred: adaptive RTO, FOTA, persistence, authentication. Deduplication is
RAM only. Power integrity remains unmeasured.
</file>

<file path="arq/STANDARDS.md">
# Standards mapping

เป็นการประยุกต์แนวคิด reliability สำหรับ raw LoRa ไม่ใช่ CoAP/TCP/UDP
หรือ LoRaWAN implementation. Sources checked 2026-11-13.

| Source | Adaptation | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [RFC 7252 §§4.2–4.8](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7252.html#section-4.2) | One outstanding confirmable exchange, randomized initial interval, exponential retransmission, duplicate ACK replay, bounded retries and exchange lifetime | `sender.c`, `receiver.c`, core assertion harness |
| [RFC 6298 §3](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6298.html#section-3) | Karn-style exclusion of RTT after retransmission; no adaptive estimator yet | Sender `attempts==1` sample guard; RTT sample counts |
| [RFC 8085 §3](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8085.html#section-3) | Conservative pacing (3 seconds), retransmission backoff; control traffic never recursively acknowledged | Sender start spacing and receiver DATA-only gate |
| [RFC 1982 §3](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc1982.html#section-3) | Modular sequence increment; exact equality rather than ordering distant sequence values; all timer intervals below half-range | Wrap tests; config timer-bound validation |
| [LoRaWAN L2 1.0.4 §§4.3.1.2–4.3.1.3](https://lora-alliance.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/LoRaWAN-Link-Layer-Specification-v1.0.4.pdf) | Compare confirmed-frame ACK and bounded retransmission concept only | Separate ACK/NACK frames in custom 12-byte header |

ไม่มี LoRaWAN receive windows, network server, join, MIC, encryption, ADR,
frame counter inference หรือ regional MAC behavior. Session IDs isolate old
traffic but do not authenticate peers. The 75 ms guard and 2–3 s RTO are
experiment settings, not RFC-mandated LoRa timings.
</file>

